	"VersionName": "1.0.0",
	"FriendlyName": "TickLedger - The Tick That Never Ran",
	"Description": "PrimaryActorTick.bCanEverTick is a wish, not a guarantee. An actor can carry bCanEverTick = true and still have no registered tick function - and then Tick() never runs, there is no error, and nothing appears in the log. It happens whenever the flag is turned on after registration already went past: in a Blueprint parent, in a construction script, from a data table. Measured on a real actor: two identical probes, one registered and one not, both with bCanEverTick = true; after ten world ticks the registered one counted 1 tick and the other 0. TickLedger watches every actor and component in the running world and records, for each one, whether it was EVER registered and EVER enabled - not the state at the end, because an object that ticked for a while and was switched off later did its job. It separates 'wants to tick but never registered' from 'registered but never enabled': the first is a wiring mistake, the second is usually deliberate. It runs where the editor cannot: in a packaged build and on a build server, with 0 clean / 1 warnings / 2 errors.",
	"Category": "Code Plugins",
	"CreatedBy": "Silvan Teufel",
